The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
void free_extra_chunks(struct hep_desc* h)
{
    ...
    if (h->version < 3 || h->u.hepv3.chunk_list == NULL)
        return;
    ...
}
```
Reason:
The `free_extra_chunks` function was registered as a context free function, which caused it to be called automatically during SIP message processing. This led to double freeing of memory when the function was invoked inappropriately, especially when messages were not SIP messages, resulting in memory leaks.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
// Original hep context free function is not registered
// but called manually after all hep processing is done.
```
Reason:
By not registering the `free_extra_chunks` function as a context free function and instead calling it manually after all processing is complete, the patch ensures that memory is only freed when appropriate, thus preventing double freeing and addressing the memory leak issue.

